    "memory is the harness process; for an in-process target it includes the dataset and oracle (see memory.before_target)",
    "io_per_query.rchar counts bytes returned by read syscalls, including page-cache hits; read_bytes counts only device reads and is near zero when the working set is cached",
    "recall is measured against a brute-force oracle computed in the harness; ties at the k-th distance may count as misses"
  ]
}
